# agnos_emit_probe — exercises the AGNOS ring-3 ABI so `_agnos_emit_gate`
# (programs/checks/ts.cyr) can assert that `CYRIUS_TARGET_AGNOS=1` emits a valid
# agnos binary: a `write`(syscall 1) to stdout + a non-zero exit, so the gate
# verifies the agnos exit epilogue (`syscall(0)`, NOT Linux `60`/`0xB8 0x3C`)
# and a valid ELF64 at entry ≥ 0x200000 (agnos's user-range floor).
# Mirrors programs/efi_probe.cyr's role for the EFI gate. See CHANGELOG [6.0.49].
#
# Kept MINIMAL on purpose: the no-Linux-60 check byte-scans the whole binary, so
# a larger probe risks a coincidental `0xB8 0x3C 00 00 00` match. The io.cyr x*
# substrate is exercised by its own `agnos_xsys_probe.cyr` + `_agnos_xsys_gate`.
include "lib/syscalls.cyr"

fn main() {
    sys_write(STDOUT_FD, "agnos-ok\n", 9);
    return 42;
}
